x360-native local patch 0004 for rexglue-sdk f5337cdc947ff6d4c4196737e2c807a48f2a1fc2 (v0.10.0)

ReXApp::OnDestroy: shut the runtime down before destroying the window.

OnDestroy destroyed the window (window_.reset()) and then the runtime. After a
successful setup the input drivers are attached to the window (AttachWindow in
ConstructRuntime), and ~MnkInputDriver, run from InputSystem::Shutdown inside
~Runtime, detaches from it through window->app_context(). The SDL window is
destroyed without OnClosing to its listeners, so the driver still held the
destroyed window: access violation in WindowedAppContext::IsInUIThread
(under a debugger) or STATUS_HEAP_CORRUPTION, whenever the app quit by itself
(dash.xex 2.0.17559.0 after its main thread returned).

The runtime is now reset while the window still exists, and the window last.
The graphics device keeps its dependencies: the overlays, the ImGui drawer and
the immediate drawer are released and the presenter is detached from the
window before, as they were. A failed setup (patch 0002) takes the same order.

Test: tests/sdkcheck/app_shutdown_test.cpp (sdkcheck.* in ctest) runs
tests/shutdown_probe, a minimal ReXApp, on a synthetic XEX whose entry point
returns: without a GPU plugin, with the xenos (D3D12) plugin, and with a setup
that fails after the graphics system was handed over.
No upstream equivalent at the time of writing (development bd833a2 has the same
order in OnDestroy).

diff --git a/src/ui/rex_app.cpp b/src/ui/rex_app.cpp
index b94fe9e..ae55246 100644
--- a/src/ui/rex_app.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/rex_app.cpp
@@ -602,8 +602,14 @@ void ReXApp::OnDestroy() {
     window_->RemoveInputListener(this);
     window_->RemoveListener(this);
   }
-  window_.reset();
+  // patch 0004: the runtime goes first, while the window still exists. After a
+  // successful setup its input drivers are attached to the window (AttachWindow in
+  // ConstructRuntime) and ~MnkInputDriver detaches from it; the SDL window is
+  // destroyed without OnClosing to its listeners, so destroying it first left the
+  // driver with a dangling pointer. Nothing made from the graphics device is left by
+  // now: the drawers were released and the presenter detached from the window above.
   runtime_.reset();
+  window_.reset();
 }
 
